# UI system — PokeSlider

## Source of truth

- **Tokens:** `src/styles/design-tokens.css` — spacing, radii, shadows, blur, motion durations, fluid type, surfaces, type atmosphere CSS variables.
- **Tailwind theme extensions:** `src/index.css` `@theme` (fonts, legacy color aliases).
- **Utilities:** `.app-focus-ring`, `.app-surface-glass`, `.motion-carousel-halo`, `.sr-only` patterns in `index.css`.

## Tailwind usage

- Prefer **semantic spacing** via CSS vars: `px-[var(--space-section-x)]`, `rounded-[var(--radius-3xl)]`.
- Text sizes: `text-[var(--text-body)]` pattern where fluid scale matters.
- Avoid reintroducing **stacked glow** filters on the carousel — use token shadows (`--shadow-carousel-active`).

## Components

- **TypeBadge** — uses `TYPE_GRADIENT` from `utils/typeGradients.ts`; keep borders subtle for contrast.
- **AsyncFeedback** — supports `role` prop (`alert` vs `status`); use `status` for non-errors.

## Atmosphere

- `AppAtmosphere` subscribes to Pokémon detail query when overlay is on Pokémon panel; sets `data-atmosphere` on `<html>`.
- Do not drive atmosphere from unrelated UI without updating `DECISIONS_LOG.md`.

## Modals & glass

- Dialog bodies: `app-surface-glass` + border `white/12` range; sticky headers use translucent `bg-[rgb(6_8_14/0.55)]` + blur token.

## Don’t

- Add a second global design token file — extend `design-tokens.css`.
- Use arbitrary neon glow chains on text-heavy panels.
